From da00218e9bd1d857764dc5ee617e90532f25cd08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vincent <vincent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 06:04:40 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] provider: MiniMax (China) presets point at api.minimax.cn,
 which answers as the old host did (#3669, kshq1996)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The vendor moved its China site off api.minimaxi.com, and the preset still
gave it, so a new MiniMax (China) provider was saved with a host the vendor
no longer serves. The preset now has api.minimax.cn for Chat, Anthropic and
the Website and KeysURL pages, and the Responses endpoint the vendor
documents at the same base as Chat (platform.minimax.cn/api-reference/
responses-create, GeneYu404 on the issue).

The host is matched by name in two more places, and both follow it:
`inlineThink` (chat.go) so a CN reply's <think> block still goes out as
reasoning and back in the assistant's text, and `planQuotaSourceOf`'s host
switch (planquota.go), which now takes api.minimax.cn as well as
api.minimaxi.com and api.minimax.io — a provider saved before the move keeps
the old host and still gets its plan card.

Tests first, both red on the base:

    $ go test -tags nogui ./internal/gateway/ -count=1 -run TestMiniMaxThinkingGoesBackInTags
    minimax_think_test.go:102: MiniMax-M2.7 at api.minimax.cn: assistant content "Hello!", want "<think>…
    $ go test -tags nogui ./internal/provider/ -count=1 -run 'TestPlanQuotaSource|TestPlanQuotas'
    planquota_test.go:50: {Provider:… Chat:https://api.minimax.cn/v1 …}: got "" ok=false sure=false
    planquota_test.go:362: cards: map[glm/home…  (no minimax-cn card)

With both fixes the same two commands pass, the whole provider package passes
(`go test -tags nogui ./internal/provider/ -count=1 -skip
TestUnreadLoginsWriteErrorsKeepCredentials` → ok, 42s; that test aborts the
run with a synctest fatal error at this base too, before and after), and the
gateway package's run shows only the five failures it has at the base. gofmt,
`go vet -tags nogui ./internal/provider/ ./internal/gateway/` and `go build
-tags nogui ./...` are clean.
---
 internal/gateway/chat.go               | 2 +-
 internal/gateway/minimax_think_test.go | 1 +
 internal/provider/planquota.go         | 2 +-
 internal/provider/planquota_test.go    | 5 +++--
 internal/provider/presets.go           | 7 +++++--
 5 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/internal/gateway/chat.go b/internal/gateway/chat.go
index da6dfe7b..7f48ed92 100644
--- a/internal/gateway/chat.go
+++ b/internal/gateway/chat.go
@@ -330,7 +330,7 @@ func buildChat(r *Request, model, host string, rejectTemp bool) []byte {
 	// interleaved thinking): the decoder takes it out as thinking (#1267),
 	// so it goes back in where it came from. A relay serving MiniMax's
 	// models may give the thinking apart and take it back otherwise.
-	inlineThink := strings.HasSuffix(host, "minimax.io") || strings.HasSuffix(host, "minimaxi.com")
+	inlineThink := strings.HasSuffix(host, "minimax.io") || strings.HasSuffix(host, "minimaxi.com") || strings.HasSuffix(host, "minimax.cn")
 	// Gemini wants each step's thought signature back on its first call
 	// (#687), and one it can't check for a step it didn't sign
 	gemini := geminiCompat(host, model)
diff --git a/internal/gateway/minimax_think_test.go b/internal/gateway/minimax_think_test.go
index f6875a9c..e1eacc50 100644
--- a/internal/gateway/minimax_think_test.go
+++ b/internal/gateway/minimax_think_test.go
@@ -88,6 +88,7 @@ func TestMiniMaxThinkingGoesBackInTags(t *testing.T) {
 	for _, c := range []struct{ model, host, want string }{
 		{"MiniMax-M2.7", "api.minimax.io", "<think>\nThe user greets me.\n</think>\n\nHello!"},
 		{"MiniMax-M2.7", "api.minimaxi.com", "<think>\nThe user greets me.\n</think>\n\nHello!"},
+		{"MiniMax-M2.7", "api.minimax.cn", "<think>\nThe user greets me.\n</think>\n\nHello!"},
 		{"minimax/minimax-m3", "openrouter.ai", "Hello!"},
 		{"kimi-k3", "api.moonshot.cn", "Hello!"},
 	} {
